// Lesson 6.1 — Gravity & Jump: The First Flick
// Unit 6 opens in the cave. Nothing in the starter jumps: PlayerController.cs is
// the student's own file from 1.4 onward, and the Rigidbody2D built in 2.1 was
// tuned for a top-down world with Gravity Scale 0. So this lesson is two new
// mechanisms, and at level 1 each gets its own walkthrough: turning gravity on
// for ONE scene, and the flick that leaves the ground.
//
// GROUND TRUTH (verified by reading the project, its scenes and its ProjectSettings):
//   - Unity 6000.6.0f1. Legacy Input class, so Input.GetKeyDown is correct.
//     Rigidbody2D.linearVelocity, not the old `velocity`.
//   - EditorBuildSettings orders the scenes Start(0), Overworld(1), Platformer(2)
//     — "the cave is index 2" is real, and SceneSwitch.cs holds a serialized int
//     build index, not a name.
//   - Physics2DSettings ships m_Gravity {x: 0, y: -9.81}, so Gravity Scale really
//     is a multiplier on it.
//   - Player.prefab READ AS A PREFAB: root Transform + PlayerController; the
//     SpriteRenderer and Animator live on a child called `Sprite`. There is NO
//     Rigidbody2D and NO Collider2D on it — those are the student's work from 2.1.
