    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Gravity Is a Number You Own</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Real gravity is a constant of the universe. Unity ships it as an <em>Inspector field</em>. Why would a game engine make a law of physics editable per object?</li>
            <li>Same Player prefab, same script, two worlds: the hub needs Gravity Scale 0 and the cave needs it above 0. Where should that difference live — the script, the scene, or both?</li>
            <li>A Kinematic body ignores gravity, forces and mass entirely. Set Body Type to Kinematic in the cave, and what would your jump code have to do instead to look like a jump?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

